tyle="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">(<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usdPerShare" contextRef="c-7" decimals="2" sign="-" name="us-gaap:EarningsPerShareDiluted" scale="0" id="f-2302">2.25</ix:nonFraction>)</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/></tr><tr style="height:14pt"><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:3pt double #000;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:3pt double #000;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:3pt double #000;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:3pt double #000;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Anti-dilutive shares</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="c-5" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareAmount" scale="3" id="f-2303">35</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="c-6" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareAmount" scale="3" id="f-2304">136</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="c-1" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareAmount" scale="3" id="f-2305">36</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="c-7" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareAmount" scale="3" id="f-2306">136</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/></tr></table><span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"></span></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:5.2pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;position:relative;top:-2.8pt;vertical-align:baseline">(1) &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">For any periods ending with a net loss, anti-dilutive financial instruments are excluded from the calculation of GAAP diluted earnings per share.</span></div></ix:nonNumeric><div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Basic net income (loss) per share is computed by dividing income (loss) available to common stockholders by the weighted-average number of common shares outstanding for the period. Diluted net income (loss) per share reflects the potential dilution that could occur if securities or other contracts to issue common stock were exercised or converted into common stock or resulted in the issuance of common stock that then shared in the net income (loss) of the Company. The computation of diluted</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">per share does not assume conversion or exercise of securities that would have an anti-dilutive effect on net income (loss) per share.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Securities issued by the Company that could potentially dilute net income (loss) per share in future periods include stock options and restricted stock.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">To calculate diluted net income (loss) per share, the Company utilizes the treasury stock method which results in only an incremental number of shares added to shares outstanding during the period.</span></div></ix:nonNumeric><div style="height:42.75pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><div><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:36.765%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:29.309%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:30.626%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #dbdbdb;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"><div><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:232%">Eagle Bancorp, Inc Second Quarter 2026 Form 10-Q &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;               </span></div></td><td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #dbdbdb;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #dbdbdb;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"><div style="text-align:right"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">38</span></div></td></tr></table></div></div></div><div id="i675c2c82ae05446f8dac57350c9b3ac1_67"></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:42.75pt;width:100%"><div><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:15.128%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:6.940%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:74.632%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"><div><span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%;text-decoration:underline"><a style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%;text-decoration:underline" href="#i675c2c82ae05446f8dac57350c9b3ac1_7">Table of Contents</a></span></div></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"><div style="text-align:right"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements | Note&#160;10&#160;&#8211; Other Comprehensive Income (Loss) </span></div></td></tr><tr style="height:3pt"><td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #dbdbdb;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #dbdbdb;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #dbdbdb;padding:0 1pt"/></tr></table></div></div><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="egbn:OtherComprehensiveIncomeLossTextBlock" id="f-2307" continuedAt="f-2307-1" escape="true"><div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"><span style="color:#192168;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:14pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note&#160;10&#160;&#8211; Other Comprehensive Income (Loss)  </span></div